  "_comment_sfqr": "Optional - Data Studio (Snowflake pane). Anything left out falls back to the 'snowflake' section above, so a minimal setup can be just allow_writes. Use either password or private_key_path, not both. The nested 'sqrn_write' block is only for deployments where reads and writes are two different logins - leave it out and everything runs on the one login, as before. When it is present, the Table Copier browses target databases with it and writes with it; if that login cannot read the source, the copier moves the rows through the portal instead of running a single INSERT inside Snowflake (clone is not possible in that case). Credentials in 'sqrn_write' are taken as a set: name a password or a private_key_path there and only those are used.",
  "snowflake_query_runner": {
    "account": "abc12345.us-east-1",
    "user": "SVC_SMARTHUB",
    "password": "",
    "private_key_path": "C:/keys/smarthub_rsa_key.p8",
    "private_key_password": "",
    "role": "SMARTHUB_RW",
    "warehouse": "SMARTHUB_WH",
